# Base URL for the Fantasy Decision Intelligence backend API.
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT - leave this empty (as below).
# An empty value makes the API client issue relative requests, which
# the Vite dev server proxies to http://127.0.0.1:8000 for /api and
# /health (see vite.config.ts). Because the browser only ever talks to
# the dev server's own origin, no CORS configuration is needed locally.
#
# PRODUCTION (Vercel) - do NOT set it in this file. Set it as a Vercel
# project Environment Variable so it is baked into the build:
#
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://fpl-intelligence-agent.onrender.com
#
# The dev proxy does not exist in a production build, so this must be
# an absolute URL. The backend must also allow this frontend's origin -
# set CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS on Render to the Vercel URL (see app/cors.py
# and the repository root .env.example).
#
# If this is left unset in production the client falls back to relative
# requests against the Vercel domain, which has no API, and every
# request fails with a 404.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
